# Connector credentials for literature-search-extract.
#
#   copy .env.example .env      (PowerShell / cmd)
#
# Then fill in only the lines for connectors you actually want to turn on, and
# save. Nothing else is needed: the next `python probe.py --id <name>` will
# start reporting `present (N chars)` instead of `absent`.
#
# THE AGENT CANNOT READ THIS FILE ONCE IT IS NAMED `.env`.
# ~/.claude/hooks/secret_file_guard.py denies Read/Grep/Bash/PowerShell access
# to it in every permission mode, so you can add a key with the agent not in
# the room, and no key can reach a transcript, a session archive, or a compact
# digest. Debugging a 401 has exactly one move here: run the probe.
#
# This template is git-tracked (see the negation in ~/.claude/.gitignore).
# The `.env` you create from it is not, and never was — the ignore rules for
# `.env` predate this file.
#
# Each variable below corresponds to a `needs_user` entry in registry.json;
# `python probe.py --list` prints what each one unlocks and what it costs.

# --- OpenAlex -------------------------------------------------------------
# Mandatory since 2026-02-13; without it you get 100 credits/day then HTTP 409.
# Free key: https://openalex.org/settings/api  (100,000 credits/day)
# Highest value-per-effort item here: one free form, and it restores a channel
# the skill currently degrades past on every run.
OPENALEX_API_KEY=

# --- Unpaywall ------------------------------------------------------------
# No key — an email address IS the credential, and it is sent with every
# request. That makes it a privacy choice, not a technical one.
# Unlocks: legal open-access full text from a DOI, i.e. [abstract] -> [full].
UNPAYWALL_EMAIL=

# --- Crossref polite pool -------------------------------------------------
# Same shape as above: an email, sent on every call, in exchange for more
# reliable metadata resolution. Optional; Crossref works without it.
CROSSREF_MAILTO=

# --- Semantic Scholar -----------------------------------------------------
# Optional and NOT blocking: the API works unauthenticated. A key buys a
# GUARANTEED 1 req/s instead of a shared pool that is throttled under load —
# a floor, not a raise.
S2_API_KEY=

# --- IEEE Xplore ----------------------------------------------------------
# Needs a registered developer account. Note the two-stage trap recorded in
# registry.json: the key alone buys metadata + abstracts; [full] additionally
# needs the institutional subscription behind it. The probe must report which
# of the two is live, because that failure is otherwise silent.
# The VPN itself is not the agent's business: it never drives the VPN and never
# sees this value. It calls a script that succeeds or fails.
IEEE_API_KEY=

# --- Institutional proxy (EZproxy / Shibboleth) ---------------------------
# LEAVE EMPTY unless you have decided this is acceptable. A session cookie is
# both a credential and a personal identity, and bulk automated fetching
# through an institutional proxy gets accounts suspended. If you do enable it,
# the safe shape is a fetch-ONE-document CLI with a hard rate cap, never a
# general proxy — and that CLI does not exist yet.
PROXY_SESSION=
